{"_id": "Finance_and_Economics--insurance_policy--p--58399", "text": "{\n    \"policy_id\": \"POL12345\",\n    \"policy_holder\": {\n        \"name\": \"Alice Johnson\",\n        \"address\": \"123 Main St, Los Angeles, CA 90001\",\n        \"contact_info\": \"alice.johnson@email.com\"\n    },\n    \"coverage_amount\": 650000.0,\n    \"premium\": 1200.5,\n    \"claim_history\": [\n        {\n            \"claim_id\": \"CLM001\",\n            \"date\": \"2023-03-15\",\n            \"amount\": 5000.0,\n            \"status\": \"Approved\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"policy_terms\": \"This policy provides comprehensive coverage for a wide range of incidents, including but not limited to fire, theft, and natural disasters. It details specific exclusions, deductible amounts, and claim procedures. The policyholder is responsible for maintaining the property in good condition. In the event of a claim, the policyholder must submit a written notice within 30 days of the incident. The policy also outlines the process for dispute resolution and arbitration. Further, it covers liability for damages to third parties. This policy is subject to annual review and may be adjusted based on market conditions and risk assessments. The coverage includes personal property up to the specified coverage amount.  Detailed descriptions of covered events and limitations are provided within this document. The insurer reserves the right to deny coverage if fraudulent information is provided.  The policyholder must comply with all applicable laws and regulations. This agreement shall be binding upon both parties. A full list of contact information for claims assistance and policy support is included in the appendix.\"\n}"}
