{"_id": "Finance_and_Economics--insurance_policy--n--65205", "text": "{\n    \"policy_id\": \"P987654321\",\n    \"policy_holder\": {\n        \"name\": \"Bob Williams\",\n        \"address\": \"456 Elm Street, Anytown, CA 91234\",\n        \"contact_information\": \"bob.williams@email.com\"\n    },\n    \"coverage_amount\": 600000.0,\n    \"premium\": 800.0,\n    \"claim_history\": [\n        {\n            \"claim_id\": \"C001\",\n            \"date\": \"2023-01-15\",\n            \"amount\": 500.0,\n            \"description\": \"Water damage\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"policy_terms\": \"This is a very comprehensive policy detailing various scenarios and clauses related to property damage, liability, and personal injury. It is essential to read and understand the entirety of these terms. Specifically, the policy outlines procedures for filing claims, dispute resolution mechanisms, and cancellation policies. Furthermore, it provides definitions for key terms used throughout the document, ensuring clarity and avoiding ambiguity. The policy also includes a section on regulatory compliance, outlining adherence to state and federal laws. In addition, the insurance provider reserves the right to modify terms and conditions with reasonable notice to policyholders. This policy also details coverage limits and exclusions, specifying what is and is not covered under the policy. The policy will also be periodically updated to comply with changing laws and regulations.\"\n}"}
