{"_id": "Finance_and_Economics--insurance_policy--p--67492", "text": "{\n    \"policy_id\": \"POL12345\",\n    \"policy_holder\": {\n        \"name\": \"Alice Johnson\",\n        \"address\": \"123 Main St, Anytown, USA\",\n        \"contact\": \"alice.johnson@email.com\"\n    },\n    \"coverage_amount\": 75000.0,\n    \"premium\": 450.0,\n    \"claim_history\": [\n        {\n            \"claim_id\": \"CLM001\",\n            \"date\": \"2023-03-15\",\n            \"amount\": 1500.0,\n            \"description\": \"Wind damage to roof\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"policy_terms\": \"This policy provides comprehensive coverage for various perils including fire, theft, and natural disasters. It outlines the responsibilities of both the insurer and the insured, detailing claim procedures, coverage limitations, and policy cancellation terms. Specific exclusions apply to acts of war and intentional damage. The policy also includes a section on dispute resolution and arbitration. This policy aims to offer maximum protection to the policyholder and ensure a transparent and fair claims process.  The insured is responsible for maintaining the property in a reasonable state of repair.  Details regarding deductibles and co-insurance are clearly explained within.  The policy term is one year, renewable annually.  Renewal rates are subject to change based on risk assessment. A complete list of covered perils is included in Appendix A. Contact customer support for any clarifications. The policy also details the process for making changes to the policy during the term.\"\n}"}
{"_id": "Finance_and_Economics--insurance_policy--n--67492", "text": "{\n    \"policy_id\": \"POL67890\",\n    \"policy_holder\": {\n        \"name\": \"Bob Williams\",\n        \"address\": \"456 Oak Ave, Anytown, USA\",\n        \"contact\": \"bob.williams@email.com\"\n    },\n    \"coverage_amount\": 60000.0,\n    \"premium\": 600.0,\n    \"claim_history\": [],\n    \"policy_terms\": \"This is a basic insurance policy covering fire and theft. Please see the full details of the coverage.  Claims must be filed within 30 days.\"\n}"}
